{
 "_comment": "Measured palette for the visual wave (task V0-05). Derived numbers only: no image from references/ is committed. Rects are pixel boxes in the named crop of the private reference set (aylmer-madness/references/places, gitignored, CMP_REF_ROOT).",
 "version": 1,
 "date": "2026-10-06",
 "conditions": "noon, clear to hazy, on-screen sRGB after the game grade. Street View frames are May and June 2009 (a few are tiles refreshed 2021 to 2024, flagged).",
 "method": {
  "per_sample": "median RGB of the pixels inside the rect that pass the colour mask, restricted to the luminance percentile band (lit surfaces 60 to 90, mid 40 to 60, deep shade 15 to 45) so shadows from trees and eaves do not drag sunlit surfaces down.",
  "per_material": "srgbTarget is the per-channel median of the per-reference medians; spread is the largest channel range between references; tolerance is max(8, largest channel std), capped at 40.",
  "albedo": "linearAlbedo = linear luminance of srgbTarget divided by the assumed noon illuminance (1.05 on horizontal faces, 0.90 on vertical faces), clamped to 0.03 to 0.80 (white vinyl 0.75). It is a first-pass seed for V1-01, not physics: Street View is display-referred and its camera exposes high.",
  "crosscheck": "Gemini gemini_analyze was attempted on three refs and failed headless (command permission auto-denied). The cross-check was done by eye against grid overlays of the same crops, and against the agreement between independent refs (spread field). Re-run the Gemini pass interactively if wanted.",
  "roadmapRule": "Where a ref cannot give the value (clipped whites, thin poles, no night or golden refs, no Ranger), the roadmap hex is retained and flagged in targetSource."
 },
 "albedoLimits": {
  "min": 0.03,
  "max": 0.8,
  "whiteVinylMax": 0.75
 },
